7: ERROR: mixed keyed/keyless sorts in the select block (L4) — `0.a^.b*` is a star branch whose landing and its sibling branches' do not agree: one level assembles a Map OR a tuple, never both. A star's landing follows its CONTENTS: Map contents splice in as KEYED fields, vector contents land as ONE KEYLESS component, and under `*` a key surviving before the star keeps the join nested under it. Here every branch is ordinal-headed, and under an ordinal head a star's landing passes through only when nothing between the ordinal and the star names a key; any other ordinal-headed branch is ONE keyless tuple component, whatever its `^`s. So make every branch a tuple component: keep a key before each star, written `*` (`x{0.a.b* 1.a.b*}`, a tuple of records), or end the branch with `^` instead of its star (`x{0.a^.b^ 1.a^.b^}`). Selecting the flatten in its own block always works
8: ERROR: mixed keyed/keyless sorts in the select block (L4) — `0.a^.b*` is a star branch whose landing and its sibling branches' do not agree: one level assembles a Map OR a tuple, never both. A star's landing follows its CONTENTS: Map contents splice in as KEYED fields, vector contents land as ONE KEYLESS component, and under `*` a key surviving before the star keeps the join nested under it. Here every branch is ordinal-headed, and under an ordinal head a star's landing passes through only when nothing between the ordinal and the star names a key; any other ordinal-headed branch is ONE keyless tuple component, whatever its `^`s. So make every branch a tuple component: keep a key before each star, written `*` (`x{0.a.b* 1.a.b*}`, a tuple of records), or end the branch with `^` instead of its star (`x{0.a^.b^ 1.a^.b^}`). Selecting the flatten in its own block always works
9: ERROR: duplicate output key `:k` in the select block — two branches deliver the same output key, and distinct keys are required (strict merge; the alternative is a silent last-write-wins). The key may be one a branch NAMES, or one a star (`*`) LIFTED out of its layer. Rename an UNSTARRED branch with `^k'` (`x{k^k2}`) — a starred segment cannot carry a rename — or select the flatten in its own block. Dropping the star of ONE ordinal-headed branch trades the collision for a keyed/keyless mix (L4): without its star that element lands as one keyless tuple component. Dropping it on every branch here gives a tuple of the elements. Through an ordinal, a star whose remainder names no key lands its fields at this level (Q_U61), so an element's lifted fields meet the level's other keys. A provenance star cannot tell elements apart: an ordinal contributes no name to a `*_` / `*-_` prefix. To keep each element as its own tuple component, end EVERY branch here with `^` instead of its star, where its last step is a key (`x{0.a^.b^ 1.a^.b^}`).
