25: ERROR: mixed keyed/keyless sorts in the select block (L4) — `a.b*-` is a star branch whose landing and its sibling branches' do not agree: one level assembles a Map OR a tuple, never both. A star's landing follows its CONTENTS: Map contents splice in as KEYED fields, vector contents land as ONE KEYLESS component; a total collapse (`*-`) always lands at its branch's top. So make the level agree — if the `*-` lands keyed, stop dissolving its siblings (drop a `^`, as in `x{a.b*- c}`); if it lands keyless, dissolve the keys that survive on the others (a `^` on each, as in `x{a.b*- c^}`). Selecting the flatten in its own block always works
